WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.260
Welcome to the Singularity Daily, Thursday edition.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.930
Here are the last 24 hours in superintelligence, in 3 minutes.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.320
Heads in the clouds? Try space.

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:21.640
SpaceX just got the go-ahead for a million AI satellites.

00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:26.310
Rival Amazon had called it a lofty ambition rather than a real plan.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:32.530
Meanwhile,

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:37.840
Anthropic's Dario Amodei says the claim he'd hand our free will to AI is absurd.

00:00:38.910 --> 00:00:42.060
His line in the sand? AI that improves itself.

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:44.670
'We may want limits on this process.'

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:49.170
And Amazon, which has blocked Meta's shopping agent Muse,

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:51.600
is reportedly talking about letting it in.

00:00:52.970 --> 00:00:55.230
Talking AI doom over Thanksgiving dinner?

00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:57.600
The New York Times wrote a guide for that.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.390
Now, the money. AI stocks took a beating for a second day,

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:06.580
and Anthropic dipped to $74.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:13.980
Still, JPMorgan expects the S&P 500 to hit 8,200 next year, thanks to AI.

00:01:14.060 --> 00:01:18.530
Anthropic's listing also made about 5,100 of its staff millionaires,

00:01:18.530 --> 00:01:19.780
at least on paper.

00:01:22.030 --> 00:01:25.010
And AI voice maker ElevenLabs is reported

00:01:25.010 --> 00:01:27.990
ly in early talks at a $33 billion value.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:34.700
A historian asked ChatGPT who drew a sketchbook from 1808.

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:37.690
22 minutes later: a French nobleman.

00:01:37.970 --> 00:01:40.950
And OpenAI's model designed new proteins.

00:01:40.950 --> 00:01:44.800
In lab tests, 35 of them latched onto their targets.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:49.580
The catch? New York just banned AI chatbot toys for five years.

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:53.910
And EA brought back the late John Motson's voice with AI,

00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:55.470
with his family's consent.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:58.370
So... is it so over?

00:01:59.060 --> 00:02:00.450
We're so back!

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:07.950
In China, XPeng showed off Iron, a humanoid with over 1,500 touch sensors.

00:02:07.970 --> 00:02:12.350
Early next year it starts training as a shop assistant in XPeng's own stores.

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:16.960
Musk says robot demos are often staged.

00:02:16.960 --> 00:02:21.410
So Figure moved the table. Its robot still found the apple.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:24.040
So keep your head in the clouds, by all means.

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:25.930
Just keep your feet on the ground.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.670
Every day, the curve gets a little steeper.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.780
Somehow, the future keeps landing early.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.370
That's one day of news. Imagine what a year looks like.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.230
That's the Singularity Daily for today.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:50.120
Same time tomorrow?

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:55.430
Want the whole month? Hear more tomorrow night.
